<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sotho people</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Southern Sotho, Basotho, Basuto</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Basotho are a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantu-peoples">Bantu-speaking</a> people of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> who speak Sesotho, living mainly in Lesotho and in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>'s Free State and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gauteng">Gauteng</a> provinces. The Basotho nation was formed in the 1820s and 1830s by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moshoeshoe-i">Moshoeshoe I</a>, who gathered refugees from the wars of the period around his mountain stronghold of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thaba-bosiu">Thaba Bosiu</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sotho-people.jpg" alt="Sotho people" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: See File history below for details. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Lesotho.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
